{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/caps/cross-read.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T09:58:30.441126Z","id":"aee18f03f11cc59b3612e2806bf5b1c4e85aada60b8ee03d1138f7923e72154c","body":{"detail":"While the daemon answers the stream but a single refetch times out, the source app's snapshot can stay stale until B's next change or the stream's next ready. The page's own db subscriptions retry after RETRY_MS and poll every POLL_MS while the stream is down; port that logic here if stale cross-app snapshots show up in use.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":136},"end":{"line":141},"content_hash":"2ffc45b02bf3af4d3477b6835de2a5b2a2620f01f4c8151e6494bf761bb59040"},"summary":"A db.artifact(id) subscription whose refetch fails unavailable waits for the next doc event, ready or resync: no retry backoff and no outage poll, unlike the page's own subscriptions in web/shell/src/caps/db.ts (RETRY_MS, POLL_MS)","tags":["W3","deferred","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/caps/cross-read.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T09:58:30.441196Z","id":"b72b4452c404f6ccd348755aca31f83791badd26f971526c693b56747202a81c","body":{"detail":"The bridge (web/bridge/src/caps/db.ts makeDb, active set) counts both kinds against one 64 for an honest page; a page that talks to the shell directly can hold 64 of each. Each source app adds one stream topic (docs:<B>?reader=<A>), bounded by db.read's 16 IDs.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":192},"end":{"line":192},"content_hash":"511d681aca548961bc00b3b9c4675e6f2f722ebdd8950507cadc8cd4a965e31f"},"summary":"Subscriptions to other apps are capped at MAX_SUBSCRIPTIONS on their own, beside the page's own cap in web/shell/src/caps/db.ts, so the shell holds up to 2 x 64 per view","tags":["W3","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/caps/cross-read.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T09:58:30.441224Z","id":"44415b8019adb146027a3212e7d0baa2bff4da3e64410a6d1c46acd767d5882e","body":{"detail":"The `asked` map (line 45) keeps one answer per source per CapabilityHost. Refetches of a live subscription never ask (read(..., mayAsk=false)), so a grant revoked while the page runs ends the subscription with not_granted instead of raising a dialog.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":88},"end":{"line":92},"content_hash":"5795cbafe3c3447f007acfbeca9b3951ba185d746a88c65b910411aca71ecd64"},"summary":"The consent dialog's dismissal (Escape, outside click) counts as Don't allow for the rest of the view: db.artifact(id) reads of that source reject not_granted without asking again until the view reloads","tags":["W3","design","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/caps/cross-read.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T10:04:13.717816Z","id":"6d87e525b2a72dee5b4691e97daf25aa575438d3b448eab97f499e5b6a316225","body":{"detail":"subscribe tests subs.size >= MAX_SUBSCRIPTIONS (line 192), then awaits current() (line 195), then subs.set (line 197). A page that posts many db.read subscribe calls with distinct sub IDs at once (the bridge's own 64 cap, web/bridge/src/caps/db.ts active set, is bypassed by posting to the shell directly) gets every one: a scratch vitest firing 200 concurrent {op: 'subscribe', artifact: B, sub: 's<i>', spec: {kind: 'doc', path: 'runs/r1'}} against crossRead with an allowing fetch saw 200 fulfilled. Each one then refetches B on every matching doc event and on every ready/resync, so the page can make the daemon serve unbounded reads of B per change. The bound stated in b72b4452 (2 x 64 per view) does not hold. The consent boundary is unaffected: every request still carries the view's reader and checked paths.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:a8c8dc35","span":{"start":{"line":188},"end":{"line":201},"content_hash":"dcc42c3d61ccaa46b8a4fa1963bfc181995cfbcfd287a2c86cf5eb46be153662"},"suggested_fix":"Count in-flight subscribes against the cap: reserve the sub ID in a pending set synchronously before the await (and release it on failure), or check the cap again after the await and refuse resource_exhausted.","summary":"The cross-read subscription cap is checked before the consent read is awaited and the subscription is stored after it, so concurrent subscribe calls all pass the check: one view can hold any number of db.artifact(id) subscriptions","tags":["review","W3","resources","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/caps/cross-read.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T10:04:13.717913Z","id":"9d2edfb165254c5c1bc4ede57085c0e1093453d63deb07f7f9b61388ce46bad2","body":{"detail":"reset/leave run endAll over subs (line 171), but a subscribe awaiting its first read (line 195) is not yet in subs; when it resolves it checks only disposed (line 196), then subs.set, watch(topicOf(src)) and env.post. A scratch vitest calling subscribe, then cr.reset(), then awaiting the subscribe saw the watch still live and one snapshot posted. The subscription then lives until the next reset or dispose, refetching B for a document that never asked for it. The page's own subscriptions in web/shell/src/caps/db.ts store the spec synchronously before the await (subscribe case), so reset drops them; the consent wait makes the cross-read path different. Same artifact and same consent, so no data crosses the boundary.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:a8c8dc35","span":{"start":{"line":193},"end":{"line":200},"content_hash":"05989561585165651b921fc91bc9938aed62503aeea76cd2bc067f1b3bd202e1"},"suggested_fix":"Give crossRead a generation counter bumped by reset/leave; subscribe captures it before the await and, when it changed, returns without storing, watching or posting (rejecting unavailable).","summary":"A db.artifact(id) subscribe still in flight when the frame loads a new document (reset) or leaves survives it: it stores the subscription, follows the reader topic and posts snapshots into the next document","tags":["review","W3","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/caps/cross-read.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T10:04:13.718005Z","id":"4a87f6130babc46e4d741e731affbe2dfe549cc5b556e2594fcb170d2c149791","body":{"detail":"get maps the daemon's not_declared (B's declaration lacks db) to not_granted (line 77); read (line 107) then prompts the owner in the owner shell. Allow PUTs the grant and the retried read is refused again. The page sees not_granted either way, but the owner is shown 'Let A read B's data?' for an app with no documents to share.","kind":"suggestion","ref":"git:a8c8dc35","span":{"start":{"line":76},"end":{"line":77},"content_hash":"4ecc5ee6b708ab584a2b2481fc208b736c63543fefe679db25496a86eb1e926a"},"suggested_fix":"Keep the daemon's not_declared as a separate internal signal that rejects not_granted without asking.","summary":"A source that does not declare db answers not_declared, which the shell turns into not_granted and so asks the owner for a grant that cannot make the read succeed","tags":["review","W3","ux","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/caps/cross-read.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T10:07:32.892605Z","id":"3261c373681c364721ed087d74c0b87df91d1d15f0e7b114229375515e01c11e","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:215522bf","summary":"subscribe stores its entry before the first await (cross-read.ts subscribe case), so the cap counts pending subscriptions; 'holds at most MAX_SUBSCRIPTIONS subscriptions of other apps, however many are asked for at once' fires 200 concurrent subscribes: 64 fulfilled, 136 resource_exhausted, one watch (npx vitest run shell/src/caps/cross-read.test.ts: 13 passed)","supersedes":"6d87e525b2a72dee5b4691e97daf25aa575438d3b448eab97f499e5b6a316225","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/caps/cross-read.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T10:07:32.892995Z","id":"82fcec9dbdb1575d7539e532dc2e3636771fb6e942cc55ae65edc3dc30027a58","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:215522bf","summary":"Each subscribe holds its own entry object as its token; reset, leave and unsubscribe remove it, and the subscribe rejects unavailable when its entry is no longer the one under its ID. 'drops a subscribe still waiting on its first read when the frame resets or leaves' checks no watch and no snapshot for both reset and leave (npx vitest run shell/src/caps/cross-read.test.ts: 13 passed)","supersedes":"9d2edfb165254c5c1bc4ede57085c0e1093453d63deb07f7f9b61388ce46bad2","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/caps/cross-read.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T10:07:32.893592Z","id":"ede81efe9fb0f7af80fac12c4d477411f4629422e02b8de5e09398ebd215127f","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:215522bf","summary":"The daemon's not_declared stays not_declared, and ask() reads the source's declaration (GET /api/artifacts/<B>) and throws not_declared without a dialog when it lacks db. 'keeps not_declared from a source without db, and never asks for a grant that cannot help' covers granted and ungranted readers: no prompt, no PUT (npx vitest run shell/src/caps/cross-read.test.ts: 13 passed)","supersedes":"4a87f6130babc46e4d741e731affbe2dfe549cc5b556e2594fcb170d2c149791","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/caps/cross-read.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T10:07:32.893919Z","id":"987f6cee41694dc9159b8de6b5802bf64b228f61e338ffffa65037ea521af7d9","body":{"detail":"The slot is reserved synchronously before the consent read (subscribe case), so concurrent calls cannot pass the cap. The bridge (web/bridge/src/caps/db.ts makeDb, active set) counts both kinds against one 64 for an honest page. Each source app adds one stream topic (docs:<B>?reader=<A>), bounded by db.read's 16 IDs.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":205},"end":{"line":205},"content_hash":"511d681aca548961bc00b3b9c4675e6f2f722ebdd8950507cadc8cd4a965e31f"},"summary":"Subscriptions to other apps are capped at MAX_SUBSCRIPTIONS (64) per view, pending ones included, beside the page's own 64 in web/shell/src/caps/db.ts: at most 128 per view for a page that posts to the shell directly","supersedes":"b72b4452c404f6ccd348755aca31f83791badd26f971526c693b56747202a81c","tags":["W3","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/caps/gesture.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T19:40:55.697744Z","id":"3b606a25e7e8e69af41b80a969976d6569a8e0f8a5ff6307ed964a2a2c8898c5","body":{"detail":"Failure: /a/<id>?app=1 with claxHost.init and enterCommentMode(); attestPointer({pointer:1,phase:'down'}) at the press, touchStart on #p, held 600 ms, eight touchMoves over 600 ms, touchEnd, then attestPointer({phase:'up'}) as the app's runJavaScript delivers it after the WebView's touchend: clax:pick has clipError 'it was not taken'. With the same drag and the 'up' attested before touchEnd, or with a drag of under ~400 ms after the 600 ms hold, the pick is taken with quote 'Grow revenue in eve'. comment-mode.ts touchDragEnd picks synchronously on touchend, and the shell evaluates frameGesture() on clax:pick-start at once (web/shell/src/view/artifact-controller.ts), so the press attestation is stale (HOLD_MS 450 + any real drag > 550 ms) and the release attestation races the frame's postMessage. The long-press no-click fallback is safe only because it waits TOUCH_CLICK_WAIT_MS (400 ms) before picking. Whether Android WebView or WKWebView deliver the host's runJavaScript before the frame's message is unspecified.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":134},"end":{"line":152},"content_hash":"bd2ebcc88bd125d75f7944555c16b23a2bcb14862d119370e7152be524e71591"},"suggested_fix":"Do not depend on the order: in app mode let a pick start wait briefly (bounded, e.g. up to 300 ms on the test clock) for a pending release attestation of a pointer in `pressed`, or count an attested press as fresh until its release is attested (pressed set non-empty) rather than for ATTEST_MS from the press. Cover both orders in web/e2e/app-mode.spec.ts.","summary":"In app mode a hold-then-drag lasting over ATTEST_MS (1 s, press to release) is refused unless the host's 'up' attestation reaches the shell before the bridge's pick start","tags":["review","touch","gesture","app-mode","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/caps/gesture.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T20:13:31.119092Z","id":"45ce1ca3acf8c5da036f67f1182181ba10613633035d8490f734ff304674c0c5","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:29ccd4a1","summary":"Fixed: an attested press counts until its paired release (plus ATTEST_MS after it, at most HELD_MAX_MS while held), and a pick start with no counted arrival waits PICK_ATTEST_WAIT_MS (300 ms) for a pending release attestation. Evidence: web/e2e/hold-drag.spec.ts app mode, a 600 ms hold plus a 600 ms drag with the 'up' attested after touchEnd, and with it before, and a quick drag: pick taken, no clipError; an unattested drag still gets 'it was not taken' (12 passed). Unit: web/shell/src/app/host.test.ts 'takes a slow hold-then-drag's pick whose release is attested after the pick starts', 'lets a pick start wait PICK_ATTEST_WAIT_MS ...', 'starts no wait without a pending press ...' (56 passed).","supersedes":"3b606a25e7e8e69af41b80a969976d6569a8e0f8a5ff6307ed964a2a2c8898c5","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/caps/net.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:21:40.604253Z","id":"8454afd70754be6bf452b46bb98f3892e79c4e635e66266fe18584e43f377730","body":{"detail":"Grants are per artifact ID (crates/clax-core/src/store/net_grants.rs), and the app's draft (spec 2026-10-12-flutter-app-round2-design §5.1) has its own ID that the owner never grants: the inspect view answers every prompt \"Don't allow\" (web/shell/src/app/host.ts closeForInspect) and this handler does not ask there. So an app whose first screen fetches renders its error state for the agent, and tests that need the network fail. Letting a draft use its app's grant (draft_of) would expose fetched data to the agent, as cross-read refuses to (crates/clax-core/src/store/grants.rs may_read); a canned or recorded response for drafts is the other route.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":118},"end":{"line":128},"content_hash":"5db7b3e3c29aa7382885c61ad7e0f6615564070f0db6e4ea6dee89919103f833"},"summary":"A draft never fetches: its render and tests see not_granted for every net call","tags":["deferred","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
